===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A place where [[public]] [[transport]] [[bus]]es stop to allow [[passenger]]s to [[board]] or [[leave]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=15 Dec 84|volume=12|number=22|journal=Gay Community News|page=3|author=Scott Brookie|title=Closing the Baths: Where Will It End?|text="The streets are packed now," said a man named Pinky, as we sat talking on a '''busstop''' bench.}}
#* '''2011''', {{w|Rebecca Black}} featuring {{w|Patrice Wilson}}, ''[[w:Friday (Rebecca Black song)|Friday]]''
#*: Gotta get down to the '''bus stop'''
#*: Gotta catch my bus, I see my friends
# {{lb|en|education}} The [[tableau]] used in [[short division]], taught as if it were a bus stop with the digits treated as people queueing.
# {{lb|en|mathematics|informal}} "[[&#x27CC;]]": The two-lined right-angled symbol used to separate [[quotient]], [[divisor]] and [[dividend]] in [[long division]] and [[short division]]
# {{lb|en|preceded by "the"}} A [[disco]] [[dance]] popular in the 1970s and 1980s.
# {{lb|en|motorsport}} {{ellipsis of|en|bus stop chicane}}

